 "text": "Practicing for two hours every Sunday is the slowest way to learn anything. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 17. One long session feels serious, but by next Sunday most of it has faded and you spend the start just catching up. And if one Sunday gets busy, that whole week is a zero. Your brain locks in a new skill between sessions a lot of it while you sleep, so split the same time, 20 minutes a day. Piano after dinner, code before work, Spanish on your commute, 20 minutes each. Now a missed day costs 20 minutes, not a week. Send this to the friend who saves it all for the weekend. That's what Demure is for. Archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day. Tonight, Kabir and the gym membership he paid for in full. What are you saving for the weekend? The links in the bio.",
